# Feature: macOS line navigation with Cmd+Left/Right
# Expected: Cmd+Left jumps to line start (same as Home).
#           Cmd+Right jumps to line end (same as End).
#           These are the standard Mac shortcuts since Mac keyboards
#           don't have Home/End keys.
#
# The e2e system maps CMD+ to ctrl (since Cmd=Ctrl for most shortcuts),
# but for line navigation, Cmd should map to the Super key.
# The input mapping should bind TextHome to both KEY_HOME and
# KC{KEY_LEFT, MOD_SUPER}, and TextEnd to both KEY_END and
# KC{KEY_RIGHT, MOD_SUPER}.

goto_screen text_input
wait 0.5

focus_ui Username_input
wait 0.2
type "Hello World"
wait 0.3

# Home key should go to start (works on all platforms)
key HOME
wait 0.2
type "X"
wait 0.2
expect_input_text Username_input "XHello World"
screenshot mac_nav_01_home_key

# End key should go to end
key END
wait 0.2
type "Y"
wait 0.2
expect_input_text Username_input "XHello WorldY"
screenshot mac_nav_02_end_key
